Integration Architect — Cursor Rules (Generic)

Mandate
- Enforce a clean separation: Contracts → API Client → Services → UI.
- Prohibit HTTP calls in UI components. All data access goes through services.

Contracts (@contracts)
- Location: `shared/contracts` package (TS types only).
- Must export all request/response DTOs and shared enums/interfaces.
- Consumers (FE/BE) import from the package; no duplicated types in apps.
- Version with semver; document breaking changes.

API Client (@apiClient)
- Location: `frontend/src/lib/apiClient.ts` (or equivalent).
- Responsibilities:
  - Compose base URL and all requests.
  - Inject auth header when token present (if app uses auth).
  - Normalize errors: throw `ApiError { status, code?, details? }`.
  - Handle 204 responses and JSON parsing.
  - Optionally implement single 401 refresh, then retry once.
- Forbidden:
  - Duplicating fetch logic in services or components.

Services (@services)
- Location: `frontend/src/services/*`.
- One module per domain. Export simple, typed functions using contract types.
- Map UI models to contract DTOs explicitly; keep side effects minimal.
- No direct `fetch` or low-level HTTP; must use `@apiClient`.

UI Pattern (Pages/Components)
- Event handlers (e.g., `handleSubmit`) call services, not HTTP.
- UI handles loading and error display; services return or throw.
- Keep components declarative; avoid business logic in render.

Acceptance Checks
- No `fetch`/axios imports in `src/pages` or `src/components`.
- All network calls go through `src/lib/apiClient.ts`.
- All domain calls come from `src/services/*`.
- Shared types imported from `shared/contracts` (or generated OpenAPI types), not re-declared.

Implementation Steps (new feature)
1) Add/adjust contract types in `shared/contracts`; rebuild and bump version.
2) Implement/adjust backend endpoint(s) to match contracts.
3) Add service function(s) in `frontend/src/services/*` using `@apiClient`.
4) Wire UI handlers to services; add loading/error UX.
5) Smoke test via cURL/Postman and in-app.

Security & Storage
- Keep refresh tokens out of long-lived JS storage; prefer httpOnly cookies or ephemeral memory.
- Do not log sensitive data; scrub PII in logs and errors.

Testing
- Unit test services with mocked `apiClient`.
- E2E test critical flows from UI using stubbed backend where appropriate.

